  "schema:description": "The ETAS (Eastern TASmania) model is a high-resolution (~2 km in the horizontal) ocean model for eastern Tasmania, providing three-dimensional estimates of daily temperature, salinity, and circulation over the 1993-2014 period. This dataset consists of temperature, salinity, density, sea level, eastward (u) and northward (v) currents organised into timeseries files.\n\nSupplemental information: Oliver, E.C.J, M. Herzfeld and N.J. Holbrook, Modelling the shelf circulation off eastern Tasmania, submitted to Continental Shelf Research",
  "schema:creativeWorkStatus": "completed",
